Rule 1 (The shape parameter must be a 1-dimensional tensor)
{v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 1
>>
Rule 2 (The shape tensor must have int32 or int64 data type)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4
>>
Rule 3 (All elements of the shape tuple must be greater than or equal to -1)
{v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ -1
>>
Rule 4 (At most one component of the shape tuple may be -1)
{v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≠ -1 ∨ (∀j ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : j = i ∨ v_2[j] ≠ -1)
>>
Rule 5 (All elements of the shape list must be greater than or equal to -1)
{v_2 : list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ -1
>>
Rule 10 (If the input is 1-dimensional and is reshaped into a 1-dimensional tensor without shape inference, the dimension size must match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ v_2.len = 1 ∧ v_2[0] ≥ 0 then shape(v_1, 0) = v_2[0]
>>
Rule 11 (If the input is 2-dimensional and is reshaped into a 1-dimensional tensor without shape inference, the new dimension size must equal the product of the input dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2.len = 1 ∧ v_2[0] ≥ 0 then shape(v_1, 0) * shape(v_1, 1) = v_2[0]
>>
Rule 12 (1D input tensor reshaped to a 2D target shape with first dimension 1 and non-negative second dimension requires second dimension matching)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ v_2.len = 2 ∧ v_2[0] = 1 ∧ v_2[1] ≥ 0 then shape(v_1, 0) = v_2[1]
>>
Rule 13 (1D input tensor reshaped to a 2D target shape with second dimension 1 and non-negative first dimension requires first dimension matching)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ v_2.len = 2 ∧ v_2[1] = 1 ∧ v_2[0] ≥ 0 then shape(v_1, 0) = v_2[0]
>>
Rule 14 (2D input tensor reshaped to a 2D target shape with matching first dimension and non-negative second dimension requires matching second dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2.len = 2 ∧ v_2[0] = shape(v_1, 0) ∧ v_2[1] ≥ 0 then shape(v_1, 1) = v_2[1]
>>
Rule 15 (2D input tensor reshaped to a 2D target shape with matching second dimension and non-negative first dimension requires matching first dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2.len = 2 ∧ v_2[1] = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ v_2[0] ≥ 0 then shape(v_1, 0) = v_2[0]
>>
Rule 16 (3D input tensor reshaped to a 3D target shape with matching first two dimensions and non-negative third dimension requires matching third dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ v_2.len = 3 ∧ v_2[0] = shape(v_1, 0) ∧ v_2[1] = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ v_2[2] ≥ 0 then shape(v_1, 2) = v_2[2]
